course: dictionary
lesson: 13923
title: Money words: ledger
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A ledger is a book, or a computer file, where a business writes down its money. Money coming in goes in one column, and money going out goes in another. «The shopkeeper wrote every sale in the ledger.» The words sale and money are your clues: a ledger is a record of money.
explain: A ledger can also be any written record kept over time, like a list. «Mum keeps a ledger of the library books we borrow.» Here there is no money at all, so the meaning is a record, not a bank book. When you meet ledger, ask yourself: is this about money, or about a list kept over time?
explain: In money lessons, a ledger shows a balance changing. The balance is the money you have now. Add money in, take money out, and you get a new balance. Clue words like in, out, total and balance tell you that the sentence is about a ledger.
fact: A ledger is a book or computer file for recording money.
fact: Money coming in and money going out are both written in a ledger.
fact: A balance is the amount of money you have left after adding and taking away.
fact: «Keep a ledger» means to write down records regularly.
fact: «On the ledger» means written down in the record.
fact: In stories, old shops and banks keep their ledgers in big paper books.
exercise: «The shopkeeper wrote every sale in her ledger.» What is a ledger in this sentence? | A kind of bread | A pet shop | *A book for recording money | A paintbrush
exercise: A ledger shows a balance changing. What happens to the balance when money comes in? | *It goes up | It stays exactly the same every time | It disappears completely | It goes down
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a book of records in this sentence: «Keep a ledger of the money in and out.» | out | money | keep | *ledger
test: «The bank clerk checked the ledger before lunch.» What does ledger mean here? | A waiting room | *A book where money is written down | A type of cake | A bag of coins
test: A ledger can also be a written record kept over time. Which is an example? | A pirate ship on the sea | *A list of every book Maya has read this year | A kind of bike | A tent for camping
exam: When you meet the word ledger, what should you check first to understand it? | Whether it rhymes with another word | Whether it is a long word | How many letters it has | *Whether the sentence is about money or a list kept over time
